      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The six keys on the brailler correspond to the six dots on a braille cell.


    To
    write a character, you press keys simultaneously to make a shape out of them.


    For
    example, pressing 1-2-3 at the same time will create a straight line, which is
    the letter L.


    Pressing all six keys at the same time will fill out every
    cell. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
